node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
*.local

# Working material, not project documentation. The predecessor-project audits, the scaffold
# sequencing and its review are inputs to the first few commits, not a record of this project.
# The durable decisions in them get promoted into the constitution and docs/decisions/, which
# are NOT ignored — only these three paths are, so a real doc tree can land beside them.
#
# They are deliberately kept on disk rather than deleted: the plan and its review are the
# snapshot of how this repo was intended to start, and the point of comparison for how it
# actually went. Neither is maintained after the scaffold lands — going stale is the intent.
docs/extraction/
docs/scaffold-plan.md
docs/plan-review-2026-08-03.md

# Milestone records — written as each milestone lands, so the next project starts faster than this
# one did. Ignored for the same reason as the three above: they are about HOW this repo was built,
# not about what it is, and a future contributor cloning it needs the decisions rather than the
# retrospectives.
#
# ⚠️ NAMED COST, since it is a real one: gitignored means machine-local. These survive neither a
# fresh machine nor a clone, and the whole point of them is to be read by the NEXT project. They are
# reached the way CLAUDE.md reaches the predecessor — by absolute path. If a machine change is ever
# on the cards, copy the folder first; nothing else will.
docs/milestones/

# Facts about THIS computer — the toolchain's location, and the map of configuration that lives
# outside git. Ignored because a clone on another machine needs none of it and would be misled by
# all of it. It was previously inside docs/scaffold-plan.md, which is explicitly not maintained past
# RELEASE, so the only record of how to run node sat in a file scheduled to be deleted.
docs/machine.md

# Eyes-on output from scripts/shot.mjs. Working material, not keepsakes — see keepsakes/README.md.
/shots/

# Ears-on output from scripts/hear.mjs, on exactly the same terms as /shots/ above — the rendered
# cues and the music arc are how a sound is judged (0027) and are regenerated in a second.
#
# ⚠️ Added by 0095, which is the first change that made rendering the music a routine part of working
# on it: the arc alone is four megabytes, and nothing had ever stopped it being committed.
#
# ⚠️ ANY NAME AND NOT `cues-*`, BECAUSE THE OLD PATTERN ONLY COVERED THE DEFAULT `--out`.
# docs/decisions/0152-a-layer-is-heard-in-the-sum.md gave `--solo` a `--theme`, so the useful
# invocation is now per-place — `--out=nebula.wav` writes thirteen `nebula-solo-*.wav` files that
# `/cues-*.wav` does not match, and a routine `git add -A` would have committed 55 MB of them. The
# rule was never about the word `cues`; nothing in this repository ships a .wav, because every sound
# it makes is synthesised at boot.
/*.wav

# Claude Code's configuration, split by what it describes — see
# docs/decisions/0201-the-ritual-is-tracked-or-it-is-not-followed.md.
#
# `.claude/skills/` and `.claude/settings.json` are about THE PROJECT and are tracked, for the same
# reason CLAUDE.md is: a clone needs them. The two below are about THIS MACHINE and are not.
#
# ⚠️ THEY WERE PREVIOUSLY EXCLUDED THROUGH `.git/info/exclude`, WHICH IS ITSELF UNTRACKED, so a clone
# inherited the hazard without the guard. `settings.local.json` carries a snapshot of this machine's
# whole `PATH` (docs/machine.md explains why it has to), and nothing tracked stopped a routine
# `git add -A` from committing it.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/launch.json

# What the typecheck hook in `.claude/settings.json` writes its exit code to. It is the ONLY evidence
# that hook ran at all — a hook that silently never fires reports exactly what a passing one does,
# which is 0199 wearing a different hat — but it is a local log, not a record of the project.
.claude/typecheck.log
